    "wind_clock_as_written": "direction wind comes FROM, 12 = headwind, 3 = from the right",
    "wind_clock": "CORRECTED. The generator passes Angular.OClock(n) to py-ballisticcalc, whose Wind.direction_from is 0 = from behind the shooter, 90 deg (3 o'clock) = from the shooter's LEFT. So the note above ('12 = headwind, 3 = from the right') does not describe what was computed: every case's windage sign shows 3 o'clock pushing the bullet right. Each case's input.windClock is therefore converted to this repo's convention (12 = headwind, 3 = from the right) as (n + 6) mod 12; the solver's raw value is kept as input.sourceWindClock."
  },
